---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Private & Browser-Based | ConvertAnyFile" description="Use privacy-first image tools directly in your browser. Remove visible watermarks locally today, with resize, compress, crop, blur and other focused tools planned on the same platform.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Useful image edits without an upload queue.</h1><p>Focused browser-side tools for common image tasks. Remove Watermark is available as the first Preview; future tools will reuse the same local-processing and responsive editor foundation.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Image Tools</span><h2>Start with a real tool, then expand carefully.</h2><p>Only Remove Watermark has a public tool route in this Preview. Planned cards show the product direction without publishing empty SEO pages for features that do not work yet.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Browser-first foundation</span><h2>Editors and converters can share a site without sharing the wrong abstraction.</h2><p>File converters keep their existing batch queue and EngineAdapter workflow. Image Tools use a separate interactive editor layer for selection masks, previews, undo state, and visual operations while still sharing navigation, layout, privacy principles, responsive design, and SEO infrastructure.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Why separate them?</strong><p>A watermark editor needs stateful canvas interaction. A format converter needs deterministic batch input/output. Keeping those workflows separate makes both easier to test and prevents future tools from bloating the converter controller.</p></div></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
